From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 06:13:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 131/185] segacd2: sample the drive state where the read fails

Two hardware logs have reported the timeshare failing at 0300, and I
have twice read that 00 as "the drive was in state 0". It is not.
34(a5) is written only inside the DRV_INIT block, and both failing
rounds were I0 rounds -- the diagnostic arm that switches DRV_INIT off
-- so the byte was never written and kept its cleared zero.

A failure code that carries a state has to sample the state on the
failing path, not on one the diagnostic can switch off. brd_fail_stat
calls CDB_STAT itself now, still inside the swapped-in world, and
stores the nibble.

So the next 03xx discriminates. 1, 2 or 4 means the drive was live and
the sector is what never arrived -- the CDC decode side. 0 or 7 means
the drive really is dead at read time despite the wake having moved it,
which points at the swap window instead.
---
 bios/segacd2.S | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd2.S b/bios/segacd2.S
index fb077b0..2e3b54f 100644
--- a/bios/segacd2.S
+++ b/bios/segacd2.S
@@ -569,9 +569,16 @@ brd_wait_init:
         // state 2 on hardware as 0x2n, and a whole-byte compare against
         // 0x20 would have missed it.
         move.w  (a0),d0
-        move.w  d0,34(a5)               // the whole word, for the report
         lsr.w   #8,d0
         andi.w  #0x00F0,d0              // the drive's own state nibble
+        // Store the nibble, not the whole word. The low byte of the
+        // failure code is documented as "the drive state the BIOS
+        // believed at the time", and stashing the raw status word here
+        // put the low half of it -- which is not the state -- into that
+        // byte. The last log read 0300 and that 00 meant nothing.
+        move.w  d0,d1
+        lsr.w   #4,d1
+        move.w  d1,34(a5)
         cmpi.w  #0x0040,d0              // paused, ready to be read from
         beq     brd_init_done
         cmpi.w  #0x0020,d0              // and 2, which a CD boot shows
@@ -639,6 +646,24 @@ brd_fail_init:
         move.w  #2,32(a5)
         bra     brd_done
 brd_fail_stat:
+        // Ask the drive what it thinks, here, at the point of failure.
+        //
+        // 34(a5) was only ever written inside the DRV_INIT block, so on
+        // any round with the I arm off it stayed at its cleared zero --
+        // and the last two hardware logs failed on exactly such a
+        // round and reported 0300, whose 00 meant "never asked" and
+        // read like "state 0". A failure code that carries a state has
+        // to sample the state on the failing path, not on a path the
+        // diagnostic can switch off.
+        movea.l a5,a0
+        move.w  #0x0081,d0              // CDB_STAT
+        move.w  d0,50(a5)
+        jsr     0x5F22
+        move.w  (a0),d0
+        lsr.w   #8,d0
+        lsr.w   #4,d0
+        andi.w  #0x000F,d0
+        move.w  d0,34(a5)
         move.w  #3,32(a5)
         bra     brd_done
 brd_fail_read:
